      "content": "I get that there are safeguards, but that feels like a very \"official\" answer. When people point out specific vulnerabilities—like how easy it is to intercept a ballot or the issues with signature matching being inconsistent—how do you respond to that? Are those just \"concerns\" or are they legitimate flaws that could actually change an outcome?",
